ge and in the performance arts?  For whom are they meant?  In this course, taught in Spanish, students explore the rich and complex role of monologues from the perspective of rhetoric, psychology, philosophy, and performance.  Students have the chance to examine and enjoy a combination of Spanish and Spanish American plays.  From the contemporary period, students study a selected mix of short plays, casting monologues, and videos.  Students also write their own monologues with the assistance of the professor and/or perform them under the tutelage of Spanish theater actor Jose Luis Pati? Throughout the class, students focus on acquiring and delivering cultural meanings through improved pronunciation, tonality, delivery, and general presentation of oral work and performances.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "SPAN 2095.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2025SU, 2024SU, 2023SU", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 359172, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "SPAN", "catalogNbr": "2180", "titleShort": "Adv Span Writing Workshop", "titleLong": "Advanced Spanish Writing Workshop", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "EUAREA", "descr": "European Studies Area", "descrformal": "European Studies Area", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}, {"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "LALANG", "descr": "Latin America